# Firmware for the onboard BCM43455 radio (brcmfmac, SDIO).
#
# Line format: <name-in-lib/firmware/brcm> <path-in-source>
#
# The source is the Armbian repository at a pinned commit (see ARMBIAN_COMMIT
# in scripts/fetch-firmware.sh). Taken from there rather than from
# linux-firmware for one reason: the NVRAM is board-specific, and this exact
# set is the one measured working on this board
# (docs/hardware-inventory.md in marvin-research).
#
# The names in the left column are dictated by what the driver asks for:
# brcmfmac looks up <chip>-sdio.bin, <chip>-sdio.clm_blob and
# <chip>-sdio.<compatible>.txt, where compatible comes from the device tree —
# "sinovoip,bpi-m4-zero" in our case.
#
# License: Cypress/Broadcom firmware, distributed in binary form. Terms to be
# checked and recorded in docs/licensing.md — TODO(build).

brcmfmac43455-sdio.bin packages/bsp/bananapi/brcm/cyfmac43455-sdio.bin
brcmfmac43455-sdio.clm_blob packages/bsp/bananapi/brcm/cyfmac43455-sdio.1LC.clm_blob
brcmfmac43455-sdio.sinovoip,bpi-m4-zero.txt packages/bsp/bananapi/brcm/cyfmac43455-sdio.1LC.txt
